<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Mustansir Billah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1226">1226</a>–<a href="/years/1242">1242</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Al-Mustansir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Mustansir Billah was an Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> in the thirteenth century. In 1229 he issued a formal investiture to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iltutmish">Iltutmish</a>, recognising him as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindustan">Hindustan</a> and the legitimate Muslim sovereign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-asia">South Asia</a>. This caliphal recognition was a critical moment in the international legitimation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-mustansir-billah.jpg" alt="Al-Mustansir Billah" width="320" height="326" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PHGCOM · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calif_al_Mustansir_Misr_1055.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
